    <bpmn:process id="W_W1024" name="W1024. Customer Material Escrow &amp; Project Fund Management for B2B Construction Accounts" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: B2B customer (contractor, developer, government project) requests material escrow arrangement for a construction project
Frequency: ~50–80 new escrow setups/year; ~150–200 active escrow accounts at any time
Volume: 1 escrow account per project; average project value PHP 2M–50M
Owner: Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Participants: Customer (Contractor/Developer), Sales Manager, Credit Analyst, Treasury Analyst, Account Manager (B2B), Store Manager (fulfillment store)
Source: workflow W1024 — Customer Material Escrow &amp; Project Fund Management for B2B Construction Accounts</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1024_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1024_Lane1" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1024_Lane2" name="Treasury Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1024_Lane3" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1024_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1024_Lane5" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1024_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1024_Start7" name="B2B customer (contractor, developer, government project) requests material escrow…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1024_Task8" name="Escrow Request &amp; Credit Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Escrow Request &amp; Credit Assessment: Customer submits escrow request through B2B portal (W936), Pro Desk (W112), or Account Manager: (a) project details: project name, location, estimated total material requirement, project timeline (start/end date), material categories needed; (b) proposed escrow deposit amount and funding schedule; (c) Credit Analyst performs credit assessment per W886: review customer trade account history, payment behavior, outstanding AR balance, and any existing escrow commitments; (d) Credit Analyst evaluates total exposure: existing credit limit + proposed escrow commitment vs. customer&#x27;s financial capacity; (e) if escrow exceeds customer&#x27;s credit limit, require bank guarantee or increased deposit; (f) Credit &amp; Collections Manager approves or declines escrow request with conditions
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Account Manager
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1024_Task9" name="Escrow Account Setup &amp; Material Pricing Lock">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Escrow Account Setup &amp; Material Pricing Lock: Upon approval: (a) Treasury Analyst creates escrow sub-account in ERP linked to customer trade account with project identifier; (b) customer deposits funds via bank transfer (BDO, BPI, Metrobank, Chinabank) or provides bank guarantee; Treasury Analyst confirms receipt and credits escrow account; (c) Sales Manager and customer agree on material pricing schedule: (i) locked prices for core materials (steel rebar, GI sheets, PVC pipes, electrical wire) at current SRP/trade price valid for the project duration; (ii) floating prices for commodity items subject to market fluctuation (cement, sand, gravel) with agreed markup cap of +10% over locked price; (d) system generates material allocation plan: reserved inventory quantities from designated fulfillment store(s) and DC(s); (e) system creates project price book per W163 (Contract Pricing &amp; Project Price Books) with escrow-specific pricing; (f) escrow agreement signed digitally per W686 (document approval) with terms: deposit amount, material list with locked prices, release schedule, expiry date, and refund conditions
Responsible (R): Treasury Analyst / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1024_Task10" name="Material Release &amp; Escrow Draw-Down">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Release &amp; Escrow Draw-Down: Customer places material release orders against escrow as project progresses: (a) customer submits material release request via B2B portal (W936) specifying quantities and delivery date; (b) system validates: (i) requested materials are within escrow material list, (ii) quantities within remaining allocation, (iii) delivery date within project timeline, (iv) escrow balance sufficient for release value; (c) system auto-approves release if within parameters; routes to Account Manager for review if any parameter exceeded; (d) upon approval: (i) system deducts material value from escrow balance at locked price, (ii) generates sales order and delivery schedule per W164 (Staged Project Delivery), (iii) inventory allocation reduced, (iv) goods dispatched from designated store/DC; (e) system sends customer updated escrow statement: remaining balance, materials released to date, remaining allocation by category
Responsible (R): Customer / System / Account Manager
Accountable (A): Account Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1024_Task11" name="Escrow Balance Monitoring &amp; Replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Escrow Balance Monitoring &amp; Replenishment: Monthly (or upon each draw-down): (a) system calculates escrow utilization rate: (released value ÷ total deposit) × 100; (b) amber alert at 60% utilization — Account Manager contacts customer to discuss replenishment or remaining scope; (c) red alert at 80% utilization — escrow approaching exhaustion; customer must deposit additional funds or reduce remaining scope; (d) if escrow is exhausted before project completion: (i) subsequent material releases charged to standard trade account credit limit per W888 (Credit Hold Management), (ii) customer notified that locked pricing no longer applies — standard trade pricing applies; (iii) if customer has no remaining credit capacity, Account Manager escalates to Credit &amp; Collections Manager for decision: extend credit, require additional deposit, or halt releases; (e) if project timeline expires with remaining escrow balance: see step 5
Responsible (R): System / Account Manager
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 15–20 min/month per active escrow</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1024_Task12" name="Project Close-Out &amp; Escrow Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Project Close-Out &amp; Escrow Reconciliation: Upon project completion or escrow expiry: (a) Account Manager performs final reconciliation: total materials released vs. original escrow agreement; (b) if escrow balance remains (customer deposited more than consumed): (i) remaining balance refunded to customer via bank transfer within 15 business days, (ii) system generates credit note per W101, (iii) released inventory allocation returned to general availability; (c) if customer consumed more than deposited (negative balance due to price adjustments, additional materials, or quantity overruns): (i) outstanding balance transferred to trade account AR per W8, (ii) standard credit terms apply, (iii) if disputed, processed per W1022 (Trade Account Statement Dispute); (d) system generates final escrow statement and project material summary for customer; (e) Account Manager conducts post-project review per W617 (B2B Quarterly Business Review) for retention and upsell; (f) escrow sub-account closed in system; financial records archived per W256
Responsible (R): Account Manager / Treasury Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit &amp; Collections Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1024_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1024_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1024_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1024_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: must aggregate releases across locations into single project-level accounting
Owner: Credit &amp; Collections Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1024_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1024_Annotation14" targetRef="W1024_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow16" sourceRef="W1024_Start7" targetRef="W1024_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow17" sourceRef="W1024_Task8" targetRef="W1024_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow18" sourceRef="W1024_Task9" targetRef="W1024_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow19" sourceRef="W1024_Task10" targetRef="W1024_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow20" sourceRef="W1024_Task11" targetRef="W1024_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1024_Flow21" sourceRef="W1024_Task12" targetRef="W1024_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1024_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1024_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1024">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Lane5_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Lane5" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="760" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Task12_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Task12"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="805" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Start7_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Start7"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_End13_di" bpmnElement="W1024_End13"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="827" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1024_Annotation14_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Annotation14"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="970" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="845" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Flow21_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Flow21"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="845" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="845" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1024_Assoc15_di" bpmnElement="W1024_Assoc15"><di:waypoint x="340" y="970" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1092" name="W1092. Customer B2B Recurring Standing Order &amp; Scheduled Auto-Replenishment Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade account or corporate customer requests a recurring material delivery schedule, or Category Manager identifies high-frequency reorder patterns qualifying for standing order automation
Frequency: ~300–500 standing order management actions/month (quarterly reviews of the ~500–800 active orders plus modifications, suspensions and ~5–8 new setups/month; new setup, modification, suspension, review)
Volume: 1 standing order template per customer project/account
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter), Supply Chain Planner, Customer (Trade Account Manager), Category Manager
Source: workflow W1092 — Customer B2B Recurring Standing Order &amp; Scheduled Auto-Replenishment Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1092_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1092_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1092_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1092_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1092_Start4" name="Trade account or corporate customer requests a recurring material delivery schedule, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1092_Task5" name="Standing Order Setup &amp; Template Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Standing Order Setup &amp; Template Creation: (a) Sales Associate reviews customer&#x27;s order history in ERP to identify recurring purchase patterns: same SKUs ordered 3+ times in the past 90 days, consistent quantities, regular delivery cadence; (b) Associate discusses standing order option with customer: &quot;Based on your recent orders, we can set up an automatic recurring delivery of [materials] every [X days/weeks]. You&#x27;ll get guaranteed availability, locked pricing, and you won&#x27;t need to place a new order each time.&quot;; (c) customer agrees and Associate creates standing order template in ERP: (i) material list with SKU, quantity per delivery, unit of measure; (ii) delivery frequency: weekly, bi-weekly, monthly, or custom interval; (iii) delivery address(es) — may be multiple sites for contractors; (iv) pricing: locked contract price per SKU valid for 90 days (with price review/adjustment clause for commodities like cement and steel whose prices fluctuate monthly); (v) start date and end date (or ongoing until cancelled); (vi) payment terms: charged to trade account per existing credit terms per W24; (vii) auto-release or manual confirm: customer chooses whether orders are released automatically (no action required) or sent for customer confirmation 2 days before scheduled release; (viii) special instructions: site contact person, gate access code, delivery time window preference
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min per setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1092_Task6" name="System Configuration &amp; Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System Configuration &amp; Validation: (a) system validates the standing order template: (i) checks SKU availability and stock levels at the servicing DC per W31 (demand forecasting) — if lead time is insufficient for auto-replenishment, flags warning; (ii) validates pricing against current SRP and trade account contract pricing per W163 — applies the lower of locked price or current contract price; (iii) checks delivery address within store/DC delivery coverage area per W668; (iv) confirms trade account credit limit has sufficient headroom for the recurring order value per W888 (credit hold management); (v) calculates total monthly commitment and annual commitment for reporting; (b) system generates standing order agreement document: material list, quantities, prices, delivery schedule, terms and conditions (minimum commitment period: 90 days, cancellation notice: 14 days, price adjustment for commodity items: monthly review per market index); (c) customer signs agreement (digital signature via app or wet signature at store); (d) system activates standing order and schedules first auto-release
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min (system validation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1092_Task7" name="Auto-Release Execution &amp; Fulfillment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Auto-Release Execution &amp; Fulfillment: (a) per the configured schedule, system auto-generates a store replenishment order or sales order (depending on delivery type) 2–3 days before the scheduled delivery date: (i) creates order with the standing order template&#x27;s material list and quantities; (ii) reserves inventory at the servicing DC per W105 (multi-channel inventory allocation); (iii) for &quot;manual confirm&quot; mode: system sends notification to customer via SMS/email/app: &quot;Your standing order for [materials] is scheduled for release on [date]. Confirm or modify by [deadline].&quot;; (iv) for &quot;auto-release&quot; mode: order is released automatically and customer receives confirmation notification; (b) DC picks, packs, and dispatches the order per W106 (DC outbound dispatch) using the scheduled delivery route per W196 (route optimization); (c) delivery executed per scheduled route; (d) customer receives goods and confirms receipt via app, SMS, or delivery driver&#x27;s device; (e) system invoices customer: order charged to trade account per W8; (f) system updates standing order execution log: delivery date, actual quantities delivered (may differ from template if partial shipment), invoice number
Responsible (R): System / DC Operations
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Automated per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1092_Task8" name="Standing Order Modification &amp; Exception Handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Standing Order Modification &amp; Exception Handling: (a) customer may modify standing order at any time: add/remove SKUs, adjust quantities, change delivery frequency, update delivery address, or temporarily suspend; (b) modifications processed by Sales Associate at the trade counter or via self-service in the BuildRight B2B portal per W936; (c) exception scenarios: (i) SKU out of stock: system substitutes with equivalent product per W279 (product substitution rules) after customer notification; if no substitution available, line item is backordered per W56; (ii) Price increase: for commodity items (cement, steel), if market price increases &gt;5% from locked price, system alerts customer with adjusted price and requests confirmation before next release; (iii) Delivery failure: if customer refuses delivery or site is inaccessible, system reschedules delivery and notifies Trade Counter Supervisor; (iv) Credit limit breach: if cumulative outstanding balance + standing order value exceeds credit limit per W888, system holds order release and alerts Trade Counter Supervisor for credit review; (v) Seasonal suspension: customer may suspend standing order during project holidays (Christmas, Holy Week) with advance notice
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min per modification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1092_Task9" name="Quarterly Review, Performance &amp; Renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Review, Performance &amp; Renewal: (a) system generates quarterly standing order review report per customer: total orders released, fill rate (% of template quantities actually delivered), on-time delivery rate, total revenue, price variance (locked vs. current market price); (b) Trade Counter Supervisor reviews reports and contacts customers for: (i) renewal discussion: extend for another 90 days, adjust pricing, modify quantities based on project phase; (ii) upsell opportunity: customer buying cement may also need sand and gravel — add to standing order; (iii) credit review: customer payment behavior on standing orders feeds into credit limit review per W887; (c) Category Manager reviews aggregate standing order data: total committed volume by SKU, demand forecasting accuracy improvement, customer retention rate for standing order customers vs. non-standing order; (d) standing order data feeds into S&amp;OP cycle per W133 for supply planning accuracy
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Quarterly review: 15–30 min per major customer; Aggregate report: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1092_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1092_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1092_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1092_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1092_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1092_Annotation11" targetRef="W1092_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1092_Flow13" sourceRef="W1092_Start4" targetRef="W1092_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1092_Flow14" sourceRef="W1092_Task5" targetRef="W1092_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1092_Flow15" sourceRef="W1092_Task6" targetRef="W1092_Task7" />
