    <bpmn:process id="W_W1107" name="W1107. Customer Bulk Purchasing Group / Co-Op Buying Program Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer group registration request, community association inquiry, or corporate partnership proposal for bulk cooperative purchasing
Frequency: ~50–100 new group registrations/month; ~500–800 active group purchase orders/month
Volume: 1 group registration; group sizes range from 5 to 500+ members
Owner: Category Manager (Merchandising)
Participants: Category Manager, Trade Account Manager, Pricing Analyst, Store Manager (fulfillment), Customer
Source: workflow W1107 — Customer Bulk Purchasing Group / Co-Op Buying Program Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1107_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1107_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1107_Lane2" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1107_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1107_Lane4" name="Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1107_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1107_Start6" name="Customer group registration request, community association inquiry, or corporate…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1107_Task7" name="Group Registration &amp; Eligibility Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Group Registration &amp; Eligibility Verification: (a) group organizer (president, captain, authorized representative) submits registration request: group name, type (HOA, barangay, contractor co-op, religious org, OFW family group), number of participating members, estimated total project spend, and project timeline; (b) Trade Account Manager verifies: (i) group has a legitimate purpose (community improvement, individual home construction, etc.); (ii) minimum group size of 5 members; (iii) minimum estimated aggregate spend of PHP 100,000 within 6 months; (c) system creates a co-op buying group account with a unique group ID, linked to individual member loyalty accounts; (d) group agreement signed by organizer, including: pricing tier commitment, order aggregation process, delivery sharing rules, and payment terms (individual member payment or group lump sum)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1107_Task8" name="Co-Op Pricing Tier Assignment &amp; Catalog Access">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Co-Op Pricing Tier Assignment &amp; Catalog Access: (a) Pricing Analyst assigns pricing tier based on estimated aggregate spend: (i) Bronze Tier (PHP 100K–500K aggregate): 5% discount on SRP for building materials categories; (ii) Silver Tier (PHP 500K–2M): 8% discount + free delivery within 10km of store; (iii) Gold Tier (PHP 2M–10M): 12% discount + free delivery + priority stock allocation; (iv) Platinum Tier (&gt; PHP 10M): 15% discount + dedicated account manager + project pricing (W163); (b) system creates group-specific price book accessible to all linked member loyalty accounts via the BuildRight mobile app; (c) members can browse the full catalog with co-op pricing visible when logged in
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1107_Task9" name="Order Aggregation &amp; Window Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order Aggregation &amp; Window Management: (a) group organizer opens an &quot;order window&quot; (typically 1–2 weeks) during which members submit individual orders into the group&#x27;s aggregated purchase; (b) each member logs into mobile app or visits store, selects items at co-op pricing, and adds to the group order; (c) system tracks: individual member sub-orders, running total of aggregated quantities, progress toward next pricing tier threshold; (d) when order window closes, system consolidates all member orders into a single master purchase order; (e) system checks inventory availability across the fulfilling store and nearest DC; (f) if total order exceeds single-store stock, system auto-splits into multi-source fulfillment (DC + store) per W534 (multi-origin fulfillment); (g) group organizer receives consolidated order summary for final approval
Responsible (R): System / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per order window</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1107_Task10" name="Payment Collection &amp; Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment Collection &amp; Reconciliation: (a) payment model selected at group registration: (i) Individual Payment — each member pays their own sub-order via GCash, card, or cash at POS; system links payments to sub-orders; (ii) Group Fund — organizer collects member contributions externally and makes a single group payment; (iii) Hybrid — members pay individually but delivery is consolidated; (b) system tracks payment status per member: paid, pending, overdue; (c) all payments must be received before delivery is scheduled; (d) system sends automated payment reminders to unpaid members via SMS/email; (e) once all payments confirmed, system releases order for fulfillment and delivery scheduling
Responsible (R): System / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: varies by payment model</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1107_Task11" name="Consolidated Delivery &amp; Individual Member Distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consolidated Delivery &amp; Individual Member Distribution: (a) system schedules a single consolidated delivery to the group&#x27;s designated delivery point (HOA clubhouse, barangay hall, construction site); (b) delivery fee split: free for Silver+ tiers; PHP 500 flat fee for Bronze split pro-rata among members; (c) at delivery point, individual member orders are separated by packing list; (d) each member (or their representative) signs for their sub-order; (e) any discrepancies at the individual level tracked and resolved per standard returns/exchange process (W12); (f) system sends post-delivery satisfaction survey to each member; (g) loyalty points awarded to each individual member based on their sub-order value
Responsible (R): Store Operations / Delivery Team
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: delivery + 30 min for distribution</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1107_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1107_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1107_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1107_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: must handle partial fulfillment gracefully
Owner: Category Manager (Merchandising)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1107_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1107_Annotation13" targetRef="W1107_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow15" sourceRef="W1107_Start6" targetRef="W1107_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow16" sourceRef="W1107_Task7" targetRef="W1107_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow17" sourceRef="W1107_Task8" targetRef="W1107_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow18" sourceRef="W1107_Task9" targetRef="W1107_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow19" sourceRef="W1107_Task10" targetRef="W1107_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1107_Flow20" sourceRef="W1107_Task11" targetRef="W1107_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1107_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1107_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1107">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1107_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1107_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1107_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1107_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1107_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1107_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1107_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
