    <bpmn:process id="W_W1111" name="W1111. Customer Contractor Crew Registration &amp; Job Site Badge Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade/professional account customer requests crew badges for their workers, or new contractor crew member onboarding
Frequency: ~500–800 new crew registrations/month; ~5,000–8,000 active crew badges at any time
Volume: 1–20 crew badges per registration request
Owner: Trade Account Manager
Participants: Trade Account Manager, Customer (Contractor/Trade Account Holder), Store Manager (badge issuance)
Source: workflow W1111 — Customer Contractor Crew Registration &amp; Job Site Badge Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1111_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1111_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1111_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1111_Lane3" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1111_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1111_Start5" name="Trade/professional account customer requests crew badges for their workers, or new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1111_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1111_Task6" name="Crew Registration Request &amp; Authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Crew Registration Request &amp; Authorization: (a) trade account holder (contractor/business owner) submits a crew registration request: crew member full name, government ID number (Philippine driver&#x27;s license, passport, or voter&#x27;s ID), role/position (foreman, lead worker, laborer), purchasing authority level, and mobile number; (b) Trade Account Manager verifies: (i) requesting individual is the authorized account holder or signatory; (ii) account is in good standing (no overdue AR per W888); (iii) total active badges would not exceed the account&#x27;s authorized crew limit (based on account tier: up to 5 badges for Bronze, 15 for Silver, 30 for Gold, unlimited for Platinum); (c) account holder signs crew authorization form accepting responsibility for all purchases made by authorized crew members
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: 10–15 min per crew member</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1111_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1111_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1111_Task7" name="Badge Creation &amp; Permission Configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Badge Creation &amp; Permission Configuration: (a) system creates crew member profile: unique badge ID, linked trade account, photo (taken in-store via webcam or uploaded from mobile), purchasing permissions: (i) Full Authority — can purchase any item up to the account&#x27;s credit limit; (ii) Category Restricted — can only purchase from approved categories (e.g., a plumbing subcontractor is restricted to plumbing/electrical categories); (iii) Amount Limited — per-transaction limit (e.g., max PHP 10,000 per transaction) and daily limit (e.g., max PHP 30,000/day); (iv) PO-Required — can only purchase against a pre-approved purchase order number provided by the contractor; (b) badge card printed in-store (plastic card printer at customer service desk) with: photo, name, badge ID, trade account name, QR code for scanning at POS; (c) badge activated in system with effective date and expiration date (typically 1 year, renewable)
Responsible (R): System / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: 5–10 min per badge</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1111_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1111_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1111_Task8" name="In-Store Badge Usage &amp; POS Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: In-Store Badge Usage &amp; POS Verification: (a) crew member presents badge at POS for trade account purchases; (b) cashier scans badge QR code; (c) POS system displays: crew member name, photo (for cashier visual verification), trade account name, purchasing permissions, per-transaction and daily limits, any pre-approved PO numbers; (d) system validates: (i) badge is active and not expired; (ii) crew member photo matches person presenting badge; (iii) items in cart are within category permissions; (iv) transaction total is within per-transaction limit; (v) daily cumulative purchases are within daily limit; (v) trade account credit limit is not exceeded (W888); (e) if all validations pass: transaction processed on trade account; (f) if any validation fails: transaction is blocked, reason displayed, and cashier directed to contact Trade Account Manager or Store Manager
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: adds 1–2 min to POS transaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1111_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1111_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1111_Task9" name="Crew Badge Lifecycle Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Crew Badge Lifecycle Management: (a) Deactivation triggers: (i) crew member leaves contractor&#x27;s employment — account holder must notify BuildRight within 24 hours; (ii) badge lost or stolen — crew member reports to any store for immediate deactivation and reissuance; (iii) account falls into arrears (W888 credit hold) — all badges auto-suspended; (iv) suspicious activity detected (W841 refund fraud detection, W842 cash handling exception) — badge suspended pending investigation; (b) Renewal: badges expire annually; system sends renewal reminder to account holder 30 days before expiration; crew members must present updated government ID for renewal; (c) Audit trail: all badge transactions logged with timestamp, store ID, cashier ID, and items purchased; accessible by account holder via trade portal (W936)
Responsible (R): System / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1111_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1111_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1111_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1111_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1111_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: must comply with RA 10173 (Data Privacy Act)
Owner: Trade Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1111_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1111_Annotation11" targetRef="W1111_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
