    <bpmn:process id="W_W1118" name="W1118. Customer Contractor Project Bidding Support &amp; Material Quote Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade/professional account customer requests a material quote for a construction project bid, or contractor submits project plans/specifications for material takeoff
Frequency: ~300–500 material-quote project bids/month (per the W162 register) plus quick pre-bid checks across all stores and corporate trade desk
Volume: 1 project bid per request
Owner: Trade Account Manager
Participants: Trade Account Manager, Pricing Analyst, Category Manager (approval for special pricing), Customer (Contractor)
Source: workflow W1118 — Customer Contractor Project Bidding Support &amp; Material Quote Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1118_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1118_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1118_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1118_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1118_Start4" name="Trade/professional account customer requests a material quote for a construction project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1118_Task5" name="Bid Package Receipt &amp; Scope Definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bid Package Receipt &amp; Scope Definition: (a) contractor submits project bid package to Trade Account Manager: (i) project plans/blueprints (PDF or physical copy); (ii) specifications (material grades, brands required, quality standards); (iii) bill of materials (if contractor has already prepared one) or request for BuildRight to prepare one; (iv) project timeline and required delivery dates; (v) bid submission deadline; (vi) project location and delivery address; (b) Trade Account Manager reviews scope: (i) project type (residential, commercial, government, renovation); (ii) estimated project value; (iii) material categories involved; (iv) delivery logistics (single site, multi-site, staged delivery); (c) system creates a project bid support case with unique reference number
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1118_Task6" name="Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Material Takeoff &amp; Quantity Calculation: (a) Trade Account Manager (with Category Manager support for complex projects) performs material takeoff from plans: (i) structural materials: cement (bags), rebar (tons by diameter), sand/gravel (cubic meters), hollow blocks (pieces), structural steel (tons); (ii) architectural finishes: tiles (sqm + 10% wastage), paint (liters based on area × coats × coverage rate), ceiling (sqm), doors/windows (units); (iii) plumbing: pipes (linear meters by diameter), fittings (count by type), fixtures (toilets, faucets, showers — units); (iv) electrical: wire/cable (linear meters by gauge), conduits (linear meters), breakers/panels (units), switches/outlets (units), fixtures (units); (v) roofing: GI sheets (pieces/sqm), insulation (sqm), framing (linear meters), fasteners (kg); (b) for complex takeoffs (commercial/government projects), system cross-references historical takeoffs from similar completed projects (W793 project close-out data); (c) quantities verified against bill of materials (if provided by contractor) — discrepancies flagged for contractor clarification
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: 2–8 hours (varies by project complexity)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1118_Task7" name="Project Pricing &amp; Quote Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Project Pricing &amp; Quote Generation: (a) Pricing Analyst applies project pricing: (i) base price: trade account contracted price per W163 (contract pricing &amp; project price books); (ii) volume discount: progressive discount tiers for large quantities (e.g., 500+ bags cement: additional 5% off trade price; 1,000+ bags: 8% off); (iii) package discount: additional 2–3% discount if contractor commits to sourcing ≥ 80% of project materials from BuildRight; (iv) seasonal pricing adjustment: if project spans seasonal transition, lock in current pricing for first phase with price protection clause for later phases; (b) for items where BuildRight cannot be competitive (e.g., bulk sand/gravel where local quarry direct pricing is lower), Trade Account Manager identifies alternative sourcing and quotes only the items where BuildRight is competitive; (c) system generates formal material quote: (i) itemized by category with quantities, unit price, extended price, and lead time; (ii) project total with discount summary; (iii) delivery logistics and freight cost estimate; (iv) payment terms (Net 30, Net 60, or project-specific terms per W165 — project retention &amp; milestone billing); (v) quote validity period (typically 30 days); (vi) terms and conditions (pricing subject to material availability, delivery schedule subject to confirmation)
Responsible (R): System / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager (if discount exceeds standard authority)
Duration: 1–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1118_Task8" name="Quote Delivery &amp; Bid Support Follow-Up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quote Delivery &amp; Bid Support Follow-Up: (a) formal quote delivered to contractor via email and published on trade portal (W936); (b) Trade Account Manager follows up: (i) answer contractor questions about material specifications, substitutions, or alternatives; (ii) provide technical data sheets, SDS, or product certifications for bid submission; (iii) adjust quantities or specifications if contractor&#x27;s bid strategy changes; (iv) if contractor&#x27;s bid is successful, convert material quote into a project order per W164 (staged project delivery &amp; call-off orders); (v) if contractor&#x27;s bid is unsuccessful, capture feedback for future pricing competitiveness analysis
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Account Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1118_Task9" name="Bid Outcome Tracking &amp; Win/Loss Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Bid Outcome Tracking &amp; Win/Loss Analysis: (a) Trade Account Manager tracks bid outcomes: (i) total bids supported per month; (ii) win rate (% of supported bids that result in a material order); (iii) average quote value vs. order value (partial wins); (iv) lost bid analysis: was BuildRight&#x27;s pricing competitive? Were there availability issues? Did the contractor lose the project entirely or win but source elsewhere? (v) competitive intelligence captured: which competitors are quoting on the same projects, at what price levels? (b) monthly bid support performance report generated for Category Manager and Head of Trade / Account Management; (c) insights feed into: (i) pricing strategy (W40, W107); (ii) assortment decisions (W679); (iii) competitive intelligence (W130, W624)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1118_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1118_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1118_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1118_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Trade Account Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1118_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1118_Annotation11" targetRef="W1118_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow13" sourceRef="W1118_Start4" targetRef="W1118_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow14" sourceRef="W1118_Task5" targetRef="W1118_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow15" sourceRef="W1118_Task6" targetRef="W1118_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow16" sourceRef="W1118_Task7" targetRef="W1118_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow17" sourceRef="W1118_Task8" targetRef="W1118_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1118_Flow18" sourceRef="W1118_Task9" targetRef="W1118_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
