    <bpmn:process id="W_W1134" name="W1134. Customer B2B Project Retention Money Release &amp; Final Billing Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer project completion confirmation, or retention period expiry (typically 30–90 days after project completion)
Frequency: ~5–9 retention releases/month (one per project completion, at the ~65–100 completions/year register)
Volume: 1 retention release per project completion
Owner: Finance Analyst (B2B / Project Accounts)
Participants: Finance Analyst, Sales Associate (Project Liaison), Customer, Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1134 — Customer B2B Project Retention Money Release &amp; Final Billing Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1134_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1134_Lane1" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1134_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1134_Start3" name="Customer project completion confirmation, or retention period expiry (typically 30–90…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1134_Task4" name="Retention Period Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Retention Period Monitoring: (a) ERP tracks retention money held per project account: customer, project name, original contract value, total retention withheld (5–10% per agreement), retention period start date, retention period end date; (b) system generates weekly report of upcoming retention releases (within 30 days of expiry); (c) Finance Analyst reviews and initiates release process 2 weeks before expiry
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1134_Task5" name="Project Completion Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Project Completion Verification: (a) Finance Analyst contacts project liaison or customer to confirm: all materials delivered as specified, no outstanding change orders (W792), no pending quality claims, no outstanding invoices beyond retention; (b) project liaison confirms all deliveries completed and customer satisfied per W1123; (c) if customer reports issues: retention release held pending issue resolution; issue tracked per W795 (service complaint) or W820 (project BOM discrepancy); (d) if project completed satisfactorily: customer signs retention release authorization (digital or physical)
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1134_Task6" name="Final Billing Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Final Billing Reconciliation: (a) system generates project billing summary: original quotation value, approved change orders (+/-), total invoiced to date, retention withheld, payments received to date, outstanding balance; (b) Finance Analyst reconciles: total invoiced = original quotation + approved change orders; payments received + retention held = total invoiced; any discrepancy investigated and resolved; (c) if underbilling discovered (missed change order): additional invoice generated before retention release; (d) if overbilling discovered: credit note processed per W766; (e) final project P&amp;L calculated: total revenue, COGS, gross margin vs. original quotation margin
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1134_Task7" name="Retention Release Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Retention Release Processing: (a) upon verified completion and reconciled billing: Finance Analyst processes retention release; (b) retention amount released as: credit to customer account for offset against future purchases, or direct payment via bank transfer/check per customer preference; (c) system updates project account: retention released, project status = &quot;Completed — All Settled&quot;; (d) release notification sent to customer with final project statement; (e) retention release recorded in AR module for cash application
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1134_Task8" name="Project Account Close-Out &amp; Analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Project Account Close-Out &amp; Analytics: (a) project account flagged as complete in CRM; (b) project performance metrics recorded: total revenue, gross margin %, delivery on-time rate, change order count, retention % held and release timeline, customer satisfaction score; (c) metrics fed into customer scorecard for account tier review; (d) lessons learned documented for future project pricing and estimation improvement; (e) customer entered into post-project follow-up cycle per W756
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst / CRM System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1134_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1134_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1134_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1134_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-185 (ensure B2B billing &amp; receivable milestone integrity.) | - operational: Finance Analyst (B2B / Project Accounts) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Finance Analyst (B2B / Project Accounts)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
