    <bpmn:process id="W_W1147" name="W1147. Customer B2B Project Material Return Window Management &amp; Excess Inventory Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: B2B/project customer requests return of unused construction materials after project completion, or project account reconciliation identifies surplus materials
Frequency: ~300–500 project return requests/month across all stores
Volume: 5–50 line items per return; average return value PHP 15,000–80,000
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate, Customer Service Rep, Customer (Project Manager)
Source: workflow W1147 — Customer B2B Project Material Return Window Management &amp; Excess Inventory Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1147_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1147_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1147_Lane2" name="Receiving Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1147_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1147_Lane4" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1147_Lane5" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1147_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1147_Start7" name="B2B/project customer requests return of unused construction materials after project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1147_Task8" name="Return Request &amp; Eligibility Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Return Request &amp; Eligibility Verification: (a) customer (project manager or contractor) presents return request with original sales order/invoice reference; (b) sales associate looks up original project order in ERP: order date, items ordered, quantities, prices, project account; (c) system verifies return eligibility: within return window (30 days for trade, 60 days for project accounts), return value within 15–20% cap of original order, customer account in good standing; (d) system flags any items already returned from this order to prevent double-return; (e) if eligible, associate creates return authorization (RMA) in system with list of proposed return items and quantities
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1147_Task9" name="Physical Inspection &amp; Acceptance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Physical Inspection &amp; Acceptance: (a) customer brings return items to store receiving dock; (b) receiving clerk and department supervisor inspect each item: original packaging intact, no damage, no water exposure (especially critical for cement, plywood, adhesives), no signs of use (power tools not activated, tiles not cut); (c) for cement: check manufacture date — if past shelf life, return refused; for tiles: verify shade/batch matches original order (per W421); for lumber: verify no warping, staining, or insect damage; (d) accepted items scanned back into inventory as &quot;returned stock&quot; with inspection grade: A (resalable as new) or B (resalable as open-box/discount per W549); (e) rejected items returned to customer with explanation
Responsible (R): Receiving Clerk / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1147_Task10" name="Credit Note Processing &amp; Project Account Adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credit Note Processing &amp; Project Account Adjustment: (a) system generates credit note for accepted returns at original invoice price; (b) credit note applied to customer&#x27;s AR account (reduces outstanding balance) or issued as store credit per customer preference; (c) credit note linked to original project order for reconciliation tracking; (d) system updates project material cost tracking (W918): actual material cost = original order value minus return credit; (e) for retention money reconciliation (W1134): credit reduces final project bill amount; (f) BIR-compliant credit note issued per W540 requirements
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1147_Task11" name="Returned Stock Reintegration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Returned Stock Reintegration: (a) Grade A returns restocked to original shelf location; inventory system updates available quantity; (b) Grade B returns moved to open-box/discount section with appropriate markdown (W549); (c) items that cannot be restocked (damaged packaging, near-expiry) dispositioned per W91 (damaged goods disposition); (d) returned stock flagged in system for priority sale to prevent aging
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1147_Task12" name="Project Return Analytics &amp; Policy Compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Project Return Analytics &amp; Policy Compliance: (a) monthly report: return rate by project account, return value as % of original order, most commonly returned items, return reason analysis; (b) accounts exceeding 20% return rate flagged for review: potential over-ordering pattern, material estimation training recommendation, or return policy abuse investigation; (c) return data shared with merchandising team for assortment and quantity estimation tool improvement (W823); (d) quarterly return policy compliance review with finance team
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1147_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1147_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1147_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1147_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
