    <bpmn:process id="W_W1149" name="W1149. Customer Multi-Store Consolidated Purchase &amp; Single Invoice Billing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Corporate or large trade account customer requests consolidated purchasing across multiple BuildRight store locations with single invoice billing
Frequency: ~200–400 consolidated purchases/month (primarily corporate/project accounts with multi-site projects)
Volume: 2–8 store locations per consolidated purchase; average total value PHP 200,000–2,000,000
Owner: Corporate Account Manager (HQ)
Participants: Corporate Account Manager, Store Managers (participating stores), Department Supervisors, Customer (Corporate Purchasing)
Source: workflow W1149 — Customer Multi-Store Consolidated Purchase &amp; Single Invoice Billing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1149_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1149_Lane1" name="Corporate Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1149_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1149_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1149_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1149_Start5" name="Corporate or large trade account customer requests consolidated purchasing across…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1149_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1149_Task6" name="Consolidated Purchase Order Creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Consolidated Purchase Order Creation: (a) corporate account manager receives purchase order from customer specifying: material list, quantities per site, delivery addresses (one per store location), delivery schedule, and billing entity; (b) account manager creates master PO in ERP linked to corporate account with single PO number; (c) system splits master PO into store-level sub-orders based on delivery address proximity to each store: Store A fulfills Site 1, Store B fulfills Site 2, etc.; (d) each sub-order inherits master PO pricing (contract/project price book per W163), credit terms, and delivery schedule; (e) credit limit checked once at master PO level (W888) — not per store
Responsible (R): Corporate Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1149_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1149_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1149_Task7" name="Store-Level Fulfillment Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store-Level Fulfillment Coordination: (a) each participating store receives sub-order in ERP with fulfillment instructions; (b) store department supervisor picks and stages materials per sub-order; (c) delivery dispatched from each store to respective site per schedule; (d) each store&#x27;s delivery confirmed via POD in system; (e) system tracks fulfillment status per sub-order: pending, partially delivered, fully delivered, delivery exception; (f) store-level fulfillment issues (stockout, partial delivery) communicated to account manager for customer coordination
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor (per store)
Accountable (A): Store Manager (per store)
Duration: Store standard fulfillment time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1149_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1149_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1149_Task8" name="Consolidated Invoice Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consolidated Invoice Generation: (a) once all sub-orders are fully delivered (or customer confirms partial delivery acceptance), account manager triggers consolidated invoice generation; (b) system aggregates all sub-order deliveries into single invoice: line items from all stores, quantities delivered, unit prices from master PO, total amount; (c) invoice headers: single invoice number, corporate account name, master PO reference, billing entity address, payment terms; (d) store-level delivery detail available as supplementary attachment (delivery receipts from each store) but not required for payment; (e) BIR-compliant invoice generated per W540 requirements
Responsible (R): System / Corporate Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1149_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1149_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1149_Task9" name="Payment Collection &amp; Store-Level Revenue Allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment Collection &amp; Store-Level Revenue Allocation: (a) customer makes single payment against consolidated invoice; (b) payment recorded in AR module against master PO; (c) system allocates revenue to each participating store based on their sub-order delivery value (for store P&amp;L reporting per W35.10); (d) intercompany settlement if stores belong to different legal entities (per W14); (e) AR aging tracked at corporate account level (single balance) rather than per-store; (f) collection follow-up managed centrally by corporate account manager (W108) not by individual stores
Responsible (R): Corporate Account Manager / System
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1149_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1149_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1149_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1149_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1149_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: complexity: Multi-store consolidated billing requires sophisticated ERP capability
Owner: Corporate Account Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
