    <bpmn:process id="W_W1153" name="W1153. Customer B2B Standing Order Seasonal Volume Adjustment &amp; Forecast Sharing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal planning cycle (W32), or quarterly B2B business review (W617), or customer-initiated volume change request
Frequency: Quarterly adjustments; monthly monitoring
Volume: ~500–800 standing orders across ~5,200 trade accounts; ~25% require seasonal adjustment
Owner: Trade Account Manager / Category Manager (HQ)
Participants: Trade Account Manager, Category Manager, Supply Chain Planner, Customer (Purchasing Manager)
Source: workflow W1153 — Customer B2B Standing Order Seasonal Volume Adjustment &amp; Forecast Sharing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1153_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1153_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1153_Lane2" name="Supply Chain Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1153_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1153_Start4" name="Seasonal planning cycle (W32), or quarterly B2B business review (W617), or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1153_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1153_Task5" name="Seasonal Demand Forecast Solicitation from B2B Customers">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal Demand Forecast Solicitation from B2B Customers: (a) 60 days before each quarter, Trade Account Manager sends seasonal forecast request to top 500 B2B accounts (representing ~80% of standing order volume): &quot;Please provide your projected material requirements for Q[X] by category: lumber, cement, tiles, plumbing, electrical, paint, hardware, tools&quot;; (b) customer provides forecast via: B2B self-service portal (W936), email, or during quarterly business review (W617); (c) for customers who don&#x27;t respond: system generates baseline forecast using historical seasonal patterns × current standing order quantities; (d) customer forecasts collected in Demantra (fit-gap C5)
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2–3 weeks (collection period)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1153_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1153_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1153_Task6" name="Forecast Aggregation &amp; Supply Chain Integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Forecast Aggregation &amp; Supply Chain Integration: (a) Supply Chain Planner aggregates all B2B customer forecasts by SKU and quarter; (b) aggregated B2B forecast feeds into overall demand planning cycle (W31) alongside POS sales forecast and ecommerce forecast; (c) supply chain impact assessment: which SKUs will see significant volume increase? Are DCs positioned to handle the increase? Are vendor lead times sufficient? (d) if supply constraints identified (e.g., cement shortage during peak season): communicate to Trade Account Manager for customer expectation management; (e) procurement adjustments made per seasonal buy plan (W32) to pre-position stock for anticipated B2B demand
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1153_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1153_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1153_Task7" name="Standing Order Seasonal Adjustment Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Standing Order Seasonal Adjustment Execution: (a) Trade Account Manager reviews each standing order against customer forecast and seasonal pattern; (b) system proposes adjustment: &quot;Customer ABC Construction: current standing order = 100 bags cement/month. Historical Q2 seasonal factor = 1.4×. Customer forecast = 150 bags/month. Recommended adjustment: 140 bags/month.&quot;; (c) account manager confirms or overrides proposed adjustment based on customer-specific knowledge; (d) adjusted standing order quantities effective from first delivery of new quarter; (e) customer notified of adjustment via email/portal with option to modify within 7 days; (f) system updates standing order schedule and DC replenishment plan
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / System
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 3–5 min per account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1153_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1153_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1153_Task8" name="Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Forecast Accuracy">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Forecast Accuracy: (a) at end of each quarter, system compares actual B2B standing order consumption vs. adjusted quantities: over-forecast % (customer ordered less than adjusted), under-forecast % (customer ordered more than adjusted — resulted in rush orders or stockouts); (b) forecast accuracy calculated per customer and aggregated; (c) customers with &gt;25% forecast variance contacted for root cause and process improvement; (d) forecast accuracy data feeds into next quarter&#x27;s adjustment algorithm to improve baseline forecasting; (e) annual standing order seasonal adjustment performance report generated for executive review
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager / System
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1153_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1153_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1153_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1153_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1153_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Trade Account Manager / Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Account Manager / Category Manager (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
