    <bpmn:process id="W_W1180" name="W1180. Government Procurement (PhilGEPS) Bidding, Accreditation &amp; Public Sector Account Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Government agency publishes Invitation to Bid (ITB) on PhilGEPS portal; or annual PhilGEPS registration renewal; or public sector account opportunity identified by Sales Rep
Frequency: ~30–50 government bids/year; ~200–300 government POs/year across all agencies
Volume: Government procurement represents ~5–8% of total revenue for Philippine retailers; LGU, DPWH, DepEd, DND are key agencies for building materials
Owner: Government Accounts Manager
Participants: Government Accounts Manager, Sales Rep, Category Manager, Finance, Legal, Head of Trade / Account Management
Source: workflow W1180 — Government Procurement (PhilGEPS) Bidding, Accreditation &amp; Public Sector Account Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1180_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1180_Lane1" name="Government Accounts Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1180_Lane2" name="Logistics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1180_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1180_Start4" name="Government agency publishes Invitation to Bid (ITB) on PhilGEPS portal; or annual…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task5" name="PhilGEPS registration &amp; compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PhilGEPS registration &amp; compliance: (a) maintain BuildRight&#x27;s PhilGEPS registration (annual renewal): legal entity documents per W643, tax compliance certificates (BIR), business permits per W650, mayor&#x27;s permits; (b) ensure all 5 BuildRight entities are registered if needed for separate bidding; (c) maintain Product Catalog listing on PhilGEPS with current pricing; (d) Legal verifies compliance with RA 9184 eligibility requirements
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2–3 days annual renewal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task6" name="Opportunity identification &amp; bid/no-bid decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Opportunity identification &amp; bid/no-bid decision: (a) monitor PhilGEPS portal daily for relevant ITBs: filter by category (building materials, hardware, tools, electrical, plumbing), location (project delivery point), estimated budget, and deadline; (b) Government Accounts Manager evaluates each opportunity: (i) product availability — can BuildRight supply all items per W56? (ii) delivery feasibility — can we deliver to project site within required timeline per W196? (iii) margin analysis — government procurement prices are typically 10–15% below retail; is the margin acceptable? (iv) competition assessment — who else is likely to bid? (v) payment risk — agency&#x27;s payment history and budget allocation; (c) bid/no-bid recommendation to Head of Trade / Account Management
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 30 min/opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task7" name="Bid preparation &amp; submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Bid preparation &amp; submission: For approved bids: (a) prepare bidding documents: (i) PhilGEPS-compliant quotation with itemized pricing, (ii) Omnibus Sworn Statement (certifying no conflict of interest, no collusion), (iii) product samples or technical specifications if required, (iv) delivery timeline and logistics plan, (v) performance bond if required (&gt; PHP 5M projects); (b) Category Manager provides pricing authorization — government bids require Category Manager approval for non-standard pricing; (c) Finance confirms credit limit for government account per W783; (d) submit bid through PhilGEPS portal before deadline (electronic submission) or physical submission at BAC (Bids and Awards Committee) office; (e) Government Accounts Manager attends bid opening
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager / Category Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 4–8 hours/bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task8" name="Award &amp; contract management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Award &amp; contract management: (a) if awarded: receive Notice of Award from BAC; (b) review and sign Purchase Order / Contract: verify delivery terms, payment terms, specifications, penalties for non-compliance; (c) Legal reviews contract per W62 if terms deviate from standard; (d) post performance security (bank guarantee or surety bond) if required; (e) enter government PO in ERP as B2B order per W58 with government-specific terms (VAT exemption, extended payment)
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task9" name="Delivery &amp; acceptance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Delivery &amp; acceptance: (a) coordinate delivery to government project site per W196 logistics planning; (b) government inspector conducts delivery inspection and acceptance; (c) obtain Inspection and Acceptance Report (IAR) signed by government inspector — this is required for invoicing; (d) process goods receipt in ERP against government PO; (e) for multi-delivery orders: track partial deliveries against PO schedule
Responsible (R): Logistics / Government Accounts Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: Per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task10" name="Invoicing &amp; collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Invoicing &amp; collection: (a) submit invoice with IAR and delivery documents to government agency&#x27;s Accounting Division; (b) follow up on payment per government payment cycle (typically 30 days but often extends to 60–90 days); (c) for VAT-exempt purchases: ensure invoice excludes VAT and includes proper government exemption documentation; (d) escalate overdue payments (&gt; 60 days) to Head of Trade / Account Management for coordination with agency Finance Officer; (e) AR aging report per W463 tracks government receivables separately
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: Per invoice</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1180_Task11" name="Annual government account review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual government account review: (a) analyze government procurement revenue by agency, category, and margin; (b) win/loss analysis on bids submitted; (c) assess PhilGEPS market opportunity for next year; (d) identify agencies with upcoming capital projects (DPWH infrastructure program, DepEd school building program); (e) plan bid pipeline and pricing strategy for next fiscal year
Responsible (R): Government Accounts Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1180_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1180_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1180_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1180_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Government Accounts Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Government Accounts Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1180_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1180_Annotation13" targetRef="W1180_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow15" sourceRef="W1180_Start4" targetRef="W1180_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow16" sourceRef="W1180_Task5" targetRef="W1180_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow17" sourceRef="W1180_Task6" targetRef="W1180_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow18" sourceRef="W1180_Task7" targetRef="W1180_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow19" sourceRef="W1180_Task8" targetRef="W1180_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow20" sourceRef="W1180_Task9" targetRef="W1180_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow21" sourceRef="W1180_Task10" targetRef="W1180_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1180_Flow22" sourceRef="W1180_Task11" targetRef="W1180_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1180_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1180_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1180">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1180_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1180_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
