    <bpmn:process id="W_W1197" name="W1197. Government Agency &amp; LGU Annual Procurement Catalog Listing &amp; Price Registration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual government procurement catalog registration cycle (Q4 for following year); or new government agency procurement relationship
Frequency: Annual registration per agency; ~50–100 active government accounts
Volume: ~10% of revenue from corporate/institutional segment; government accounts represent ~30–40% of corporate segment
Owner: Trade &amp; Institutional Sales Manager
Participants: Trade Sales Manager, Category Managers, Pricing Analyst, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, Store Managers (government stores)
Source: workflow W1197 — Government Agency &amp; LGU Annual Procurement Catalog Listing &amp; Price Registration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1197_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1197_Lane1" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1197_Lane2" name="Trade Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1197_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1197_Lane4" name="Delivery Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1197_Lane5" name="AR Collector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1197_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1197_Start7" name="Annual government procurement catalog registration cycle (Q4 for following year); or new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task8" name="PhilGEPS registration maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: PhilGEPS registration maintenance: VP Legal &amp; Compliance ensures BuildRight Depot, Inc. maintains active PhilGEPS registration as a supplier: (a) annual renewal of PhilGEPS membership, (b) update of company documents (SEC registration, BIR tax clearance, mayor&#x27;s permit, PCAB license if applicable), (c) update of product categories served
Responsible (R): VP Legal
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task9" name="Annual catalog price preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Annual catalog price preparation: In Q4 each year, Trade Sales Manager coordinates with Category Managers and Pricing Analyst to prepare annual government price list: (a) review current government contract pricing vs. SRP, (b) apply government discount tier (typically 15–25% below SRP depending on category), (c) validate prices against market benchmarks and competitor government pricing, (d) prepare price list in government-required format (per GPPB guidelines)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 20 hours (over 2 weeks)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task10" name="Agency-specific price registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Agency-specific price registration: For key government accounts (DPWH, DepEd, DOH, DND, LGUs): (a) submit annual price quotation to agency procurement office, (b) attend pre-registration meeting/bidding if required, (c) negotiate annual volume commitments and pricing, (d) obtain approved supplier status and price registration for the fiscal year
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): COO (for &gt; PHP 10M accounts)
Duration: 4–8 hours/agency</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task11" name="Store-level government order readiness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store-level government order readiness: For stores near government installations (camps, schools, hospitals, government offices): Store Manager designates a &quot;Government Account Liaison&quot; (typically the Department Supervisor or CSR) who: (a) is trained on government purchase order requirements (PO number, fund source, SARO number if applicable), (b) knows the store&#x27;s government pricing per registered catalog, (c) maintains relationship with agency procurement officer for repeat orders
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Trade Sales Manager
Duration: 2 hours/store (one-time setup)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task12" name="Government PO processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Government PO processing: When a government agency issues a purchase order: (a) Trade Sales Manager or designated liaison validates PO against registered price list (no price deviations allowed), (b) confirms fund source and authority (SARO, allotment, or LGU budget authorization), (c) verifies delivery address and schedule (government sites have specific receiving requirements and authorized receiving personnel), (d) system creates sales order linked to government account with special billing terms (typically Net 30–60)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / Store Liaison
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30 min/PO</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task13" name="Delivery and documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Delivery and documentation: Delivery to government sites requires: (a) delivery receipt signed by authorized government receiving officer (not just any employee), (b) invoice in government-required format (with fund source, PO number, SARO number), (c) compliance with delivery schedule (late deliveries may result in PO cancellation), (d) photo documentation of delivered goods at site per W1122
Responsible (R): Delivery Driver / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Per W980 (B2B delivery)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1197_Task14" name="Collection and compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Collection and compliance: AR collection for government accounts follows strict process: (a) submit collection documents (delivery receipt, invoice, acceptance certificate) to agency accounting office, (b) follow up on processing timeline (government payment typically 30–60 days after document submission), (c) ensure BIR-compliant documentation (official receipt, withholding tax certificate — Form 2307 per W711), (d) track in AR aging per W889 with separate government account segment
Responsible (R): AR Collector / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1197_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1197_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1197_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1197_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: dedicated Trade Sales Manager and standardized document checklists; operational: conservative pricing in Step 2 that includes buffer for commodity price volatility; operational: maintaining separate AR aging for government and escalating to COO for accounts &gt; 90 days
Owner: Trade &amp; Institutional Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1197_Assoc17" sourceRef="W1197_Annotation16" targetRef="W1197_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
