    <bpmn:process id="W_W1225" name="W1225. Government Infrastructure Project Supply Bid, Pricing &amp; Award Fulfillment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Government agency or LGU publishes Invitation to Bid (ITB) for building materials supply; or BuildRight is invited as pre-qualified supplier for infrastructure project
Frequency: ~3–5 government bid opportunities/month (~30–50/year, one register with W1180); active bidding on 3–5 major projects at any time
Volume: ~120–240 bid evaluations per year; win rate ~20–30% = ~25–70 awarded contracts/year
Owner: B2B Sales Manager
Participants: B2B Sales Manager, Pricing Analyst, Supply Planning Analyst, Category Manager, Legal Counsel, Finance Manager, COO (for contracts &gt; PHP 10M)
Source: workflow W1225 — Government Infrastructure Project Supply Bid, Pricing &amp; Award Fulfillment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1225_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1225_Lane1" name="B2B Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1225_Lane2" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1225_Lane3" name="Supply Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1225_Lane4" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1225_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1225_Start6" name="Government agency or LGU publishes Invitation to Bid (ITB) for building materials supply…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task7" name="Bid identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bid identification: B2B Sales Manager monitors PhilGEPS portal and LGU procurement portals for relevant ITBs: (a) filter by category (building materials, plumbing, electrical, paint), (b) filter by project location (must be serviceable from BuildRight DC or store network), (c) filter by project value (target: PHP 5M–50M; below PHP 5M: not worth bid preparation cost; above PHP 50M: requires executive approval and may exceed supply capacity), (d) assess competitiveness: does BuildRight have price advantage vs. wholesale traders?
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task8" name="Bid/no-bid decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Bid/no-bid decision: B2B Sales Manager and Category Manager evaluate: (a) Supply feasibility: can BuildRight supply required quantities within project timeline? (check inventory + vendor capacity), (b) Price competitiveness: can BuildRight offer competitive pricing given wholesale rates and logistics costs? (c) Payment terms acceptability: government Net 60–90 acceptable for cash flow per W233? (d) Compliance readiness: all required documents current (PhilGEPS registration, tax clearance per W90, business permits per W427, audited financial statements)?, (e) Strategic value: does winning this project open doors for future government business?; document bid/no-bid decision
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 2 hours per bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task9" name="Bid preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Bid preparation (if bid approved): B2B Sales Manager coordinates bid documents: (a) Technical proposal: product specifications, compliance certifications (PS mark, ICC, ASTM standards), delivery schedule, project management approach; (b) Financial proposal: itemized pricing per bill of materials, delivery fees, payment terms; Pricing Analyst calculates competitive pricing: procurement cost from vendor + logistics cost + handling + target margin (typically lower margin than retail — 8–15% vs. 28–32% — offset by volume); (c) Compliance documents: PhilGEPS certificate, mayor&#x27;s permit, BIR tax clearance, audited financial statements, track record (list of completed government contracts), organizational chart, notarized omnibus sworn statement
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / Pricing Analyst / Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 1–3 days per bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task10" name="Bid submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Bid submission: B2B Sales Manager submits bid to Bids and Awards Committee (BAC) per RA 9184 requirements: (a) physical submission in sealed envelope (most LGU procurement still requires physical submission) or electronic submission via PhilGEPS; (b) attend pre-bid conference if required; (c) respond to BAC clarifications within prescribed timeframe
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task11" name="Post-qualification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-qualification (if lowest calculated bid): BAC may conduct post-qualification: verify BuildRight&#x27;s submitted documents, inspect warehouse/stock, confirm capability; B2B Sales Manager coordinates site visit and document presentation
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task12" name="Contract award and execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Contract award and execution: (a) BAC issues Notice of Award; (b) Legal Counsel reviews contract terms: delivery schedule, payment terms, warranty, penalties for non-performance, force majeure provisions, (c) COO approves contract (Head of Trade / Account Management for &lt; PHP 10M; COO for PHP 10M–50M; CEO for &gt; PHP 50M), (d) sign contract; post performance security (bank guarantee or surety bond — typically 5% of contract value for supply of goods (10% for infrastructure works) per RA 9184)
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel / Head of Trade / Account Management / COO
Accountable (A): COO/CEO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task13" name="Fulfillment planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Fulfillment planning: Supply Planning Analyst plans fulfillment: (a) confirm inventory availability at nearest DC; if insufficient: place special PO with vendor per W3, (b) schedule deliveries per project timeline (often phased: foundation materials first, then finishing materials), (c) coordinate logistics: dedicated truck or 3PL for project site delivery per W1191, (d) assign dedicated project coordinator at BuildRight for large projects
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst / Logistics Manager
Accountable (A): B2B Sales Manager
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task14" name="Delivery and billing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Delivery and billing: (a) DC dispatches materials per delivery schedule; Receiving Clerk at project site signs delivery receipt, (b) B2B Sales Manager submits billing documents: sales invoice, delivery receipt, acceptance certificate (signed by project engineer); government requires specific billing format per agency, (c) system tracks government receivable separately per W8 (AR aging) with extended payment terms
Responsible (R): B2B Sales Manager / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1225_Task15" name="Collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Collection: (a) Finance Manager monitors government AR aging per W889; government payment typically requires: submission of collection receipt, OR, and sometimes liquidation documents, (b) if payment delayed beyond contract terms: B2B Sales Manager follows up with agency procurement officer and accounts payable; escalate to Commission on Audit (COA) for delayed disbursement per W108, (c) Finance Manager records government collection per W99
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / B2B Sales Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1225_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1225_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1225_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1225_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: B2B Sales Manager review and approval gate
Owner: B2B Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1225_Assoc18" sourceRef="W1225_Annotation17" targetRef="W1225_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1225_Flow19" sourceRef="W1225_Start6" targetRef="W1225_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1225_Flow20" sourceRef="W1225_Task7" targetRef="W1225_Task8" />
