    <bpmn:process id="W_W1263" name="W1263. Government &amp; Institutional Emergency Procurement Rapid Response &amp; Relief Supply Fulfillment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ad-hoc — triggered by government emergency declaration (typhoon, earthquake, flood, pandemic), LGU emergency purchase order, or DSWD/DND/DPWH emergency procurement request
Frequency: As-needed; estimated 10–20 emergency procurement responses per year, concentrated during typhoon season (June–November)
Volume: Emergency orders ranging from PHP 500,000 to PHP 50M per event; typical items: cement, lumber, plywood, nails, tarps, generators, water tanks, electrical supplies
Owner: Trade Sales Manager / COO
Participants: Category Manager, DC Operations Manager, Logistics Planner, Procurement Specialist, Finance Controller, Store Manager, Government Procurement Officer
Source: workflow W1263 — Government &amp; Institutional Emergency Procurement Rapid Response &amp; Relief Supply Fulfillment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1263_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1263_Lane1" name="Trade Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1263_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1263_Lane3" name="DC Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1263_Lane4" name="Logistics Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1263_Lane5" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1263_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1263_Start7" name="Ad-hoc — triggered by government emergency declaration (typhoon, earthquake, flood…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1263_Task8" name="Emergency request receipt &amp; assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Emergency request receipt &amp; assessment: Trade Sales Manager receives emergency procurement request: (a) identify requesting agency (DPWH, LGU, DSWD, etc.) and verify authorized procurement officer; (b) confirm procurement authority — emergency procurement under RA 9184 requires declaration of state of calamity or emergency; (c) capture detailed requirement: item list, quantities, delivery location, required delivery date; (d) assess inventory availability: check on-hand at nearest stores and DCs to the affected area; (e) estimate total order value and confirm budget source (calamity fund, agency budget, international aid)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1263_Task9" name="Emergency pricing &amp; quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Emergency pricing &amp; quotation: Category Manager provides emergency pricing: (a) apply government pricing per PhilGEPS registered price list or W1197 catalog pricing; (b) for items not on catalog: apply SRP minus standard trade discount (5–15%); (c) include logistics cost for emergency delivery; (d) prepare quotation within 4 hours — emergency procurement timeline requires rapid response; (e) submit quotation with RA 9184 compliant documentation: (i) emergency justification, (ii) price reasonableness certification, (iii) agency purchase request reference
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1263_Task10" name="Order fulfillment mobilization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order fulfillment mobilization: Upon award confirmation: (a) DC Operations Manager allocates inventory from nearest DC and stores: (i) pull from DC stock first (fastest mobilization), (ii) supplement with store stock from non-affected stores in the region, (iii) emergency inter-DC transfer per W218 if needed; (b) assign emergency logistics: (i) own fleet if available, (ii) 3PL partner with expedited contract, (iii) military/government vehicle coordination for disaster areas; (c) assign Store Manager at nearest store as local coordinator for multi-drop emergency delivery; (d) target: first delivery within 24 hours of order confirmation
Responsible (R): DC Operations Manager / Logistics Planner
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1263_Task11" name="Delivery &amp; documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery &amp; documentation: Execute emergency delivery: (a) load and dispatch per emergency logistics plan; (b) delivery team obtains receiving documentation: (i) government inspection and acceptance report, (ii) delivery receipt signed by authorized procurement officer, (iii) photos of delivered goods at site; (c) for disaster areas with limited communication: pre-arrange cash-on-delivery payment terms or LGU guarantee letter; (d) update system with delivery confirmation and documentation upload
Responsible (R): Logistics Planner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 8–16 hours per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1263_Task12" name="Post-event settlement &amp; replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-event settlement &amp; replenishment: Within 7 days of delivery: (a) submit invoice and documentation to government agency per RA 9184 emergency procurement terms; (b) Finance Controller tracks emergency receivable — government payment terms typically 30 days but may be expedited for emergency procurement; (c) replenish depleted store and DC inventory from national network; (d) post-event review: document lessons learned for future emergency response — what was in stock, what ran out, what took too long
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 4–8 hours per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1263_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1263_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1263_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1263_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Trade Sales Manager / COO review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Sales Manager / COO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1263_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1263_Annotation14" targetRef="W1263_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
