    <bpmn:process id="W_W1288" name="W1288. Customer B2B Project Progress Billing &amp; Milestone Payment Collection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Construction project milestone completion or scheduled progress billing date
Frequency: ~80–120 active B2B construction projects at any time (one register with W918); ~1–3 progress billings per project
Volume: ~30–60 progress invoices per month (one register with W165/W1426); average invoice value PHP 200K–2M
Owner: Trade Account Manager
Participants: Trade Account Manager, Category Manager, AR Collector, Customer (Project Manager), Controller
Source: workflow W1288 — Customer B2B Project Progress Billing &amp; Milestone Payment Collection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1288_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1288_Lane1" name="Trade Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1288_Lane2" name="Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1288_Lane3" name="AR Collector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1288_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1288_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1288_Start6" name="Construction project milestone completion or scheduled progress billing date">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task7" name="Milestone verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Milestone verification: Trade Account Manager verifies project milestone completion with customer&#x27;s project manager: (a) review project plan and agreed billing milestones, (b) confirm which milestone has been reached (e.g., foundation complete, framing complete, electrical rough-in complete), (c) obtain written milestone confirmation (email or signed document), (d) verify material delivery status — all materials for this milestone have been delivered per W1283 and goods receipt confirmed
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task8" name="Progress invoice preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Progress invoice preparation: Trade Account Manager prepares progress invoice: (a) compile all material deliveries since last billing, (b) match deliveries to project PO and milestone allocation, (c) calculate billing amount per contract terms (milestone percentage × total contract value or actual deliveries), (d) apply any agreed pricing adjustments (volume rebates, promotional credits), (e) generate BIR-compliant progress billing invoice with project reference and milestone description
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task9" name="Invoice review and approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Invoice review and approval: Controller reviews progress invoice: (a) verify billing amount matches contract terms, (b) confirm all deliveries have goods receipt posted in system, (c) check credit limit availability for remaining project balance, (d) for government projects: verify compliance with procurement terms and required documentation (ORA, delivery receipts, acceptance certificates), (e) approve or return for correction
Responsible (R): Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task10" name="Invoice submission to customer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Invoice submission to customer: Trade Account Manager submits progress invoice to customer: (a) for private projects: email invoice with supporting delivery documents, (b) for government projects: submit through official procurement channel with required attachments (ORN, delivery receipts, inspection acceptance), (c) follow up within 5 business days to confirm receipt and payment timeline, (d) enter expected payment date in AR system for collection follow-up per W890
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task11" name="Payment collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment collection: AR Collector follows up on progress payment: (a) monitor AR aging per W889 for project invoices, (b) for private projects: follow up at Net 30 with customer&#x27;s accounts payable, (c) for government projects: follow up at Net 60 per government procurement payment cycle, (d) if payment delayed &gt;15 days beyond terms: escalate to Trade Account Manager for customer relationship intervention, (e) record payment in AR system upon receipt
Responsible (R): AR Collector
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15 min/invoice</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1288_Task12" name="Retention money tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Retention money tracking: System tracks retention money per project: (a) for each progress billing, system automatically calculates and segregates retention amount (typically 10% per billing), (b) retention balance accumulates in dedicated retention liability account, (c) system flags projects approaching completion for retention release processing per W1134, (d) retention release requires: project completion certificate, customer inspection acceptance, and retention period elapsed per contract terms
Responsible (R): System / Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 15 min/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1288_Task13" name="Project completion &amp; final billing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Project completion &amp; final billing: At project completion: (a) Trade Account Manager prepares final reconciliation: total contract value vs. total billings vs. total deliveries, (b) resolve any quantity or pricing discrepancies with customer, (c) issue final invoice including retention release if applicable, (d) update project status to &quot;Completed&quot; in CRM, (e) trigger post-project review for lessons learned and relationship development
Responsible (R): Trade Account Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1288_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1288_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1288_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1288_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: factoring government payment delays into cash flow forecasts per W589
Owner: Trade Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1288_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1288_Annotation15" targetRef="W1288_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
