    <bpmn:process id="W_W1308" name="W1308. B2B Project Bid, Tender Response &amp; Government Procurement Compliance Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Government agency, LGU, or private developer issues Invitation to Bid / Request for Quotation (RFQ) for construction materials supply; or BuildRight proactively identifies project opportunity
Frequency: ~30–50 bid opportunities/month across Philippines (government + private); BuildRight responds to ~15–25 bids/month
Volume: ~15–25 active bids in progress at any time; average bid value: PHP 2–50M; win rate: ~25–30%
Owner: Trade Sales Manager
Participants: Trade Sales Manager, Category Manager, Pricing Analyst, VP Legal &amp; Compliance, Finance Controller, Procurement Specialist, Project Coordinator
Source: workflow W1308 — B2B Project Bid, Tender Response &amp; Government Procurement Compliance Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1308_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1308_Lane1" name="Trade Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1308_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1308_Start3" name="Government agency, LGU, or private developer issues Invitation to Bid / Request for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1308_Task4" name="Opportunity identification &amp; qualification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Opportunity identification &amp; qualification: (a) Trade Sales Manager monitors bid opportunities: (i) PhilGEPS portal for government bids matching BuildRight&#x27;s product categories, (ii) developer/contractor relationship network for private project opportunities, (iii) LGU procurement portal for local government projects; (b) qualifies each opportunity: (i) project value vs. minimum bid threshold (BuildRight bids on projects &gt; PHP 500K material supply), (ii) product specification match — can BuildRight supply the specified materials from its catalog?, (iii) delivery feasibility — is the project site within BuildRight&#x27;s delivery coverage (near existing store or DC)?, (iv) payment terms risk — government projects pay slowly; does the project&#x27;s payment timeline align with BuildRight&#x27;s cash flow requirements?, (v) competition assessment — are there other major suppliers bidding?; (c) for qualified opportunities: create bid tracking record in CRM with opportunity details, estimated bid value, and bid submission deadline
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management &amp; Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1308_Task5" name="Bid preparation &amp; pricing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Bid preparation &amp; pricing: (a) Trade Sales Manager assembles bid team: (i) Category Manager confirms product availability and specifies exact item matches for project specifications, (ii) Pricing Analyst calculates competitive pricing: material cost + logistics cost + handling + margin, (iii) Procurement Specialist sources any items not in current inventory (special-order materials per W38); (b) pricing strategy: (i) for government bids: lowest compliant bid wins — price aggressively to win, relying on volume margin and vendor rebates per W1303, (ii) for private bids: competitive but value-added pricing — emphasize BuildRight&#x27;s advantages (wide assortment, reliable delivery, credit terms, project support); (c) Pricing Analyst prepares bid pricing sheet: (i) line-by-line item pricing (unit price × quantity), (ii) delivery cost estimate (per trip from nearest DC/store to project site), (iii) total bid price with VAT, (iv) alternative items (if BuildRight has a lower-cost equivalent that meets specification); (d) Finance Controller reviews bid pricing for margin adequacy (minimum gross margin target: 15% for project bids)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / Pricing Analyst / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management &amp; Operations
Duration: 4–8 hours per bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1308_Task6" name="Compliance documentation preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance documentation preparation: For government bids (per RA 9184): (a) VP Legal &amp; Compliance ensures eligibility documents are current: (i) PhilGEPS registration (renewed annually), (ii) mayor&#x27;s permit for BuildRight Depot, Inc. (current year), (iii) BIR tax clearance (current), (iv) audited financial statements (latest year — BuildRight must demonstrate financial capacity for the bid value), (v) DTI business name registration, (vi) PCAB (Philippine Contractors Accreditation Board) license — not required for material suppliers but may be required for delivery-and-install bids, (vii) Omnibus Sworn Statement (attesting to eligibility and no conflicts of interest); (b) Trade Sales Manager compiles technical proposal: (i) product technical specifications matching bid requirements, (ii) product samples or catalog pages, (iii) delivery schedule and logistics plan, (iv) project references (past projects supplied by BuildRight)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / VP Legal
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 4–8 hours per government bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1308_Task7" name="Bid submission &amp; follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Bid submission &amp; follow-up: (a) submit bid per procuring entity&#x27;s requirements: (i) government bids: submit through PhilGEPS or physical submission at BAC (Bids and Awards Committee) office before deadline, (ii) private bids: submit proposal to developer&#x27;s procurement department; (b) attend pre-bid conference (if scheduled) to clarify specifications and BuildRight&#x27;s capabilities; (c) post-submission follow-up: (i) respond to BAC requests for clarification, (ii) negotiate with private developer on terms, (iii) for government bids: attend bid opening to verify BuildRight&#x27;s bid was accepted and check competing bid prices
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management &amp; Operations
Duration: 2–4 hours per bid</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1308_Task8" name="Contract execution &amp; project kickoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Contract execution &amp; project kickoff: (a) if BuildRight wins the bid: (i) receive Notice of Award from BAC or purchase order from private developer, (ii) VP Legal reviews contract terms: delivery schedule, payment terms, penalty clauses, warranty, force majeure, (iii) Finance Controller reviews: payment milestones, credit exposure (add to customer credit limit per W100/W1300), tax implications (government projects may have different VAT treatment), (iv) execute contract — VP Legal signs for BuildRight; (b) create project delivery plan: (i) Project Coordinator schedules material deliveries from nearest DC or store per project timeline, (ii) coordinate with DC Operations Manager for material staging and delivery truck scheduling per W6, (iii) for items not in stock: Procurement Specialist places expedited PO per W2A with vendor; (c) create project billing schedule per contract terms: (i) milestone billing (deliver X cubic meters of cement, bill upon delivery), or (ii) monthly billing (cumulative deliveries for the month invoiced on 30th); (d) project added to CRM with contract value, delivery schedule, billing milestones, and assigned Project Coordinator
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / Project Coordinator / VP Legal
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management &amp; Operations
Duration: 1–2 days per project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1308_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1308_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1308_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1308_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: Trade Sales Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Trade Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1308_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1308_Annotation10" targetRef="W1308_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
