    <bpmn:process id="W_W1426" name="W1426. Trade Account Project Progress Billing, Milestone Payment Collection &amp; Retention Warranty Release" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Project milestone completion per contract; or monthly billing cycle for ongoing projects; or retention period expiry (typically 6–12 months after project completion)
Frequency: Per project milestone (varies by project); ~80–120 active trade projects at any time (one register with W918); ~30–50 milestone billings/month; ~5–9 retention releases/month
Volume: ~80–120 active trade projects (one register with W918/W165) with combined contract value of ~PHP 200–400M at any time; individual project values range from PHP 500K (small residential) to PHP 50M+ (large commercial/government)
Owner: Trade Sales Manager
Participants: Trade Sales Manager, Project Coordinator, AR Clerk, Controller, Store Manager, Trade Account Customer, Project Engineer/Architect
Source: workflow W1426 — Trade Account Project Progress Billing, Milestone Payment Collection &amp; Retention Warranty Release</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1426_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1426_Lane1" name="Trade Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1426_Lane2" name="Project Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1426_Lane3" name="AR Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1426_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1426_Start5" name="Project milestone completion per contract; or monthly billing cycle for ongoing projects…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1426_Task6" name="Project billing plan setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project billing plan setup: At project initiation per W11.2 (project sales), Trade Sales Manager establishes billing plan: (a) total project value and scope of materials, (b) billing milestones: (i) mobilization/advance billing (typically 10–20% upon contract signing), (ii) delivery milestones (e.g., 30% upon foundation materials delivered, 30% upon framing materials, 20% upon finishing materials), (iii) retention: 5–10% of total value withheld from each billing, (c) payment terms per milestone (typically Net 30 from billing date), (d) system creates project billing schedule with milestone triggers
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1426_Task7" name="Milestone verification and billing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Milestone verification and billing: When a delivery milestone is reached: (a) Project Coordinator verifies: (i) all materials for this milestone have been delivered (per delivery receipts signed by customer&#x27;s representative), (ii) customer&#x27;s project engineer/architect has accepted the materials (quality and quantity confirmation), (b) Trade Sales Manager generates progress billing invoice: (i) items delivered this milestone × contracted price, (ii) less retention holdback (5–10%), (iii) net billable amount, (c) AR Clerk posts invoice: Dr. Accounts Receivable / Cr. Revenue, (d) invoice delivered to customer with supporting delivery receipts
Responsible (R): Project Coordinator / Trade Sales Manager / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours/milestone</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1426_Task8" name="Milestone payment collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Milestone payment collection: (a) AR Clerk monitors milestone payment due dates per W1420 (monthly statement), (b) if customer does not pay within terms (Net 30): (i) Trade Sales Manager contacts customer — construction projects often have payment delays because the customer&#x27;s own financing draw is delayed, (ii) negotiate: accept partial payment + committed date for balance, (iii) if customer&#x27;s project is delayed (construction halt): discuss interim payment plan (customer pays for delivered materials even if project is paused), (c) for payments &gt; 60 days overdue: escalate per W1200 (trade account health) — consider pausing further deliveries until payment received
Responsible (R): AR Clerk / Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 1–2 hours/week per active project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1426_Task9" name="Project completion and final billing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Project completion and final billing: (a) upon project completion: (i) Trade Sales Manager reconciles total materials delivered vs. project scope — are there changes/variants? (ii) generate final progress billing: remaining materials delivered less retention, (iii) customer&#x27;s project engineer/architect provides final acceptance certificate, (b) system updates project status to &quot;Completed — Retention Pending&quot;
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1426_Task10" name="Retention release">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Retention release (T+6 to T+12 months after completion): (a) when retention period expires per contract (typically 6–12 months after project completion): (i) Trade Sales Manager confirms no material defect claims have been filed, (ii) obtain customer&#x27;s signed release form, (b) AR Clerk generates retention release invoice: Dr. Accounts Receivable / Cr. Retention Revenue, (c) collection per standard terms, (d) if customer files defect claim during retention period: (i) evaluate claim validity with Store Manager, (ii) if valid: arrange replacement materials (deducted from retention or billed separately), (iii) if invalid: provide documentation and negotiate full retention release
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Manager / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1426_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1426_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1426_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1426_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-185 (ensure B2B billing &amp; receivable milestone integrity.) | - operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Trade Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1426_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1426_Annotation12" targetRef="W1426_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1426_Flow14" sourceRef="W1426_Start5" targetRef="W1426_Task6" />
