        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1508_Lane3" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1508_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1508_Lane4" name="Project Sales Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1508_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1508_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1508_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1508_Start6" name="Customer&#x27;s project quotation (W162, W148) exceeds PHP 50,000 and customer requests…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task7" name="Financing eligibility screening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Financing eligibility screening: During project quotation per W162, if total project value exceeds PHP 50,000: (a) Sales Associate offers financing option to customer, (b) conducts preliminary eligibility check: (i) customer age 21–65, (ii) employed or self-employed with minimum monthly income PHP 25,000, (iii) valid government ID, (iv) no active loan defaults; (c) if customer interested and preliminarily eligible: proceed to application
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Project Sales Mgr
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task8" name="Application submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Application submission: Sales Associate assists customer with partner bank&#x27;s digital application: (a) select financing partner — (i) BDO/BPI: home improvement loan (12–36 month terms, 1.5–2.5% monthly add-on rate), (ii) credit card installment: 3/6/12/24/36 month terms at partner bank rates, (iii) Home Credit: in-store financing (6–48 months, higher rate, faster approval for customers without bank accounts); (b) customer completes application on partner bank tablet/QR link: personal details, employment/income information, project details, monthly budget; (c) customer uploads required documents: government ID, proof of income (pay slip or ITR for employed; business permit + bank statements for self-employed), proof of billing; (d) Sales Associate links application to BuildRight project quotation in ERP
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Project Sales Mgr
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1508_Task9" name="Credit assessment &amp; approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credit assessment &amp; approval: Partner bank performs credit assessment: (a) standard bank financing: 3–5 business days for approval; credit investigation, income verification, and credit bureau check; (b) credit card installment: instant approval if customer has existing credit card with sufficient limit; (c) Home Credit: real-time algorithmic approval (1–5 minutes) based on customer data and internal scoring; (d) approval result communicated to Sales Associate via partner bank portal and to customer via SMS; (e) if declined: partner bank provides reason (not communicated to BuildRight for privacy); Sales Associate explores alternatives: lower project scope, longer tenor, different financing partner, or cash payment with modified project plan
Responsible (R): Partner Bank / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min (instant) to 5 days (bank)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task10" name="Loan documentation &amp; project confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Loan documentation &amp; project confirmation: Upon approval: (a) customer signs loan agreement (digital or paper) with financing partner; (b) partner bank issues Loan Reference Number linked to BuildRight project quotation; (c) system updates project quotation status to &quot;Financing Approved&quot;; (d) Sales Associate confirms project schedule with customer: material procurement timeline per W164, installation scheduling per W138, and project delivery milestones; (e) customer pays any required down payment (typically 10–20% of project cost) directly to BuildRight at POS
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer / Partner Bank
Accountable (A): Project Sales Mgr
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task11" name="Disbursement &amp; revenue recognition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Disbursement &amp; revenue recognition: (a) partner bank disburses loan proceeds to BuildRight: full project amount less customer down payment; disbursement within 3–5 days of loan signing; (b) Finance records revenue: (i) full project revenue recognized at point of material delivery/service completion per PFRS 15, (ii) customer&#x27;s installment payments are between customer and bank — BuildRight receives full payment upfront from bank, (c) for credit card installments: POS processes as installment sale; MDR and interest subsidy reconciliation per FIN-045
Responsible (R): Finance (AR) / Partner Bank
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 3–5 days (bank disbursement)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task12" name="Project fulfillment monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Project fulfillment monitoring: Project Sales Manager monitors financed projects for timely completion: (a) financed projects must be completed within agreed timeline per loan terms; delays risk customer dispute and potential loan cancellation, (b) if project encounters material delays or installation issues: escalate per W792 (change order) and immediately notify customer and partner bank if timeline extension needed, (c) project completion triggers final billing reconciliation per W793
Responsible (R): Project Sales Mgr
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1508_Task13" name="Monthly financing portfolio review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly financing portfolio review: Project Sales Manager and Finance review financing program monthly: (a) application volume by store, (b) approval rate by financing partner, (c) average loan amount and tenor, (d) project completion rate for financed projects, (e) customer default rate (partner bank reports, not BuildRight&#x27;s direct exposure), (f) incremental revenue attributable to financing program vs. cash-only sales, (g) partner bank commission/rebate reconciliation
Responsible (R): Project Sales Mgr / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1508_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1508_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1508_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1508_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-273 (ensure controlled execution — Project Sales &amp; B2B (PA-11.2).) | - operational: clear consent language in digital application; operational: preliminary eligibility screening (Step 1) and offering multiple financing partners with different risk appetites; operational: dispatch-before-disbursement exceptions require Credit Manager approval with documented float-risk acceptance per occurrence
Owner: Project Sales Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1508_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1508_Annotation15" targetRef="W1508_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
